BF16 Tensor-Core QSA indexer scores v2 (fn_qsa_scores_tc / fn_qsa_scores_tc_paged)

Replaces the scalar FP32 FMA inner loop in `qsa_tile::scores` for prompt chunks
(rows >= 16, HI == 4, DI == 128) with BF16 `mma16816` Tensor Core instructions
using FP32 accumulators (64 query rows x 512 pooled blocks per CTA, 256 threads /
8 warps, cp.async double-buffered pooled keys in 87,040 B dynamic SMEM, register-only
4-head reduction with no SMEM reduction buffer), with both contiguous and paged variants.
Gated by `TF_FLASHNEXT_QSA_TC` (default 1; `0` restores scalar `qsa_tile::scores`).

Verified on GB10 (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next EXL3 4.05bpw + DFlash2, with patches 0007-0010):
- 248K cold prefill: 141.46 s (1,749.3 tok/s) -> 130.21 s (1,900.4 tok/s) (-11.25 s / +8.6%)
- 65K cold prefill: 32.52 s (2,011.5 tok/s) -> 31.69 s (2,063.9 tok/s) (+2.6%)
- Exactness: 120K needle retrieval byte-identical (sha ae38468a7f52, FALCON-9472-OMEGA),
  5/5 greedy and 5/5 T=0.7 token_sha256 identical to stock, drafts on == drafts off.

